mutual-mark-free
owner: opus-5 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: mutual recursion in a direct block needs NO mark — `!.tailcall
  (other(n))` colours through Free.directColor like any other program
  value. I reported the opposite yesterday; that report was a probe run
  against classes built BEFORE directColor landed (22:06 vs 23:14), and
  the whole position matrix compiles and runs against fresh ones
  (1 000 001 hops, 512 KB stack). So: TestDirectDeep asserts both
  spellings, the four doc sites that say `.reflect` for mutual
  recursion are corrected, and the stale-classpath trap is recorded.
files: src/test/scala/TestDirectDeep.scala, docs/direct-style.md,
  docs/theory/08-direct-style.md, specs/direct-macro.md, CHANGELOG.md
